  "body": "### Summary\nAs the team, we want a short technical spec of the survey form, so that it is built without back-and-forth.\n\n### Scope\n- Stack suited to a small VPS (the sub-domain is chosen later).\n- Data model of one answer; theme 2 shown only to iPad, Duo or multi-device profiles.\n- Formats: single choice, card sort, reaction cards, free text; every question optional.\n- End screen with live statistics; anti-duplicate without account, rate limiting, honeypot; CSV and JSON export.\n- Deployment and removal procedure. Code location: `tooling/ux-survey/` on `dev-swift`.\n\n### Deliverable\n`docs/ux/questionnaire/formulaire-spec.md`.\n\n### Model and review\nOpus author, Fable review. Brief: `docs/ux/cadrage-agents-questionnaire.md` §3, UX-09.\n\nTracked on #628.\n\n### Before you start\n\nRead, in order: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md`, `docs/agents/LESSONS.md`, then `docs/ux/README.md`. The UX documents are in French. Until the docs PR is merged into `dev-swift`, read them on branch `docs/ux-questionnaire`.\n\nRules: no proposal the PO classed **Non** may appear in the survey (`docs/ux/tri-m5-decisions.md` §3.5 and §4.7). The reader keeps the WebView: the survey only shows improvements possible with it. Stop and report if an instruction contradicts the plan.\n\n---\n_Opened with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) for the PO (Bruno), 2026-11-07._\n\n",
